From: Oscill project
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: xilinx: bound atomic polling with a delay

Linux 6.6 atomic polling without a delay charges only one nanosecond per
iteration. A one-second timeout becomes a billion AXI register reads and
keeps capture close in the kernel for minutes on Zynq. Charge at least a
microsecond per failed poll, including the corresponding atomic delay.

--- a/drivers/dma/xilinx/xilinx_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/xilinx/xilinx_dma.c
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@
 #define xilinx_dma_poll_timeout(chan, reg, val, cond, delay_us, timeout_us) \
 	readl_poll_timeout_atomic(chan->xdev->regs + chan->ctrl_offset + reg, \
-				  val, cond, delay_us, timeout_us)
+				  val, cond, (delay_us) ? (delay_us) : 1, timeout_us)
 
 /* IO accessors */
 static inline u32 dma_read(struct xilinx_dma_chan *chan, u32 reg)
 {
